      "explanation": "<p>$$f(3x) - f(x) = x$$ ...... (1)</p>\n<p>$$x \\to {x \\over 3}$$</p>\n<p>$$f(x) - f\\left( {{x \\over 3}} \\right) = {x \\over 3}$$ ....... (2)</p>\n<p>Again $$x \\to {x \\over 3}$$</p>\n<p>$$f\\left( {{x \\over 3}} \\right) - f\\left( {{x \\over 9}} \\right) = {x \\over {{3^2}}}$$ ...... (3)</p>\n<p>Similarly</p>\n<p>$$f\\left( {{x \\over {{3^{n - 2}}}}} \\right) - f\\left( {{x \\over {{3^{n - 1}}}}} \\right) = {x \\over {{3^{n - 1}}}}\\,.....\\,(n)$$</p->\n<p>Adding all these and applying $$n \\to \\infty $$</p>\n<p>$$\\mathop {\\lim }\\limits_{n \\to \\infty } \\left( {f(3x) - f\\left( {{x \\over {{3^{n - 1}}}}} \\right)} \\right) = x\\left( {1 + {1 \\over 3} + {1 \\over {{3^2}}}\\, + \\,....} \\right)$$</p>\n<p>$$f(3x) - f(0) = {{3x} \\over 2}$$</p>\n<p>Putting $$x = {8 \\over 3}$$</p>\n<p>$$f(8) - f(0) = 4$$</p>\n<p>$$ \\Rightarrow f(0) = 3$$</p>\n<p>Putting $$x = {{14} \\over 3}$$</p>\n<p>$$f(14) - 3 = 7 \\Rightarrow f(14) = 10$$</p>"
